.TH TX\-SIGN 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.2.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
tx\-sign \- sign ONE transaction after a human reads its summary and types a code on /dev/tty
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tx\-sign \-\-tx FILE (\-\-plan FILE | \-\-expect\-to ADDR [...] [\-\-max\-fee N] [\-\-policy FILE]) [\-\-call SIGNATURE]... [\-\-abi FILE] [\-\-create\-hash KECCAK] < keys   (asks for a code on the terminal)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
.RS 2
  tx\-sign \-\-tx FILE \-\-expect\-to ADDR [\-\-expect\-to ADDR]... [\-\-change ADDR]... [\-\-chain btc|ltc|doge]
          [\-\-chain\-id N (required for EVM)] [\-\-max\-fee SATS_OR_WEI] [\-\-from 0xADDR] [\-\-allow\-warnings] [\-\-allow\-value\-with\-token] [\-\-expect\-memo MEMO] [\-\-policy FILE]  < keys
.RE
.fi
\-\-expect\-memo MEMO: UTXO THORChain\-style memo. A single zero\-value OP_RETURN is accepted only when its payload
.nf
.RS 2
  equals MEMO byte\-for\-byte (UTF\-8); without it every OP_RETURN is refused (unexpected_output).
.RE
.fi
\-\-policy FILE: offline policy file (docs/POLICY.md), checked in addition to the flags, before signing and on the signed bytes.
\-\-chain is optional: the chain comes from the tx\-build file's "chain" field (a differing \-\-chain is refused).
bch/bsv/btg PSBTs are signed with the replay\-protected fork\-id sighash (SIGHASH_ALL|FORKID, BTG fork id 79;
P2PKH/P2PK, plus P2WPKH on btg; every input needs its proving prev_tx), never the BTC sighash.
The transaction (PSBT from tx\-build, a pos\-ntime or zec JSON line from tx\-build, or an unsigned EVM tx) comes from \-\-tx FILE (it is public).
EVM: legacy EIP\-155 and EIP\-1559 (type 2), byte\-exact against Trust Wallet Core's signer vectors; types 1, 3 and 4 are refused.
Keys come ONLY on stdin: one per line, WIF or 64\-hex, or JSON lines with wif/private_key/key/secret
(JSON lines without any of those fields, e.g. a reader's "done" line, are skipped).
Order: policy checks (destination, fee cap, chain id, no warnings) \-> sign in memory \-> print the
tx\-decode summary on the terminal \-> human types the code \-> re\-decode + re\-check \-> print
{"signed_tx": hex[, "psbt": finalized base64]}. Without a terminal, or with the wrong code, nothing is printed except "aborted".
EVM contract call: \-\-call SIGNATURE (repeatable) / \-\-abi FILE; the calldata must decode exactly and the
.nf
.RS 2
  decoded function and args are shown in the summary. Unknown selectors are refused (unknown_contract_call).
.RE
.fi
EVM contract creation: \-\-create\-hash KECCAK (keccak256 of the init code) instead of \-\-expect\-to; the summary
.nf
.RS 2
  shows the init code hash and the new contract address (CREATE from the signer and nonce).
.RE
.fi
Default fee cap: UTXO per chain (chain rate limit x vsize, never below 100000 sats; policy::default_fee_cap) / 0.01 ETH (EVM); raise it with \-\-max\-fee.
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
\-\-abi
\-\-call
\-\-create\-hash
\-\-expect\-to
\-\-max\-fee
\-\-plan
\-\-policy
\-\-tx
.fi
Each flag's meaning is in the SYNOPSIS usage line(s) above (taken from \-\-help).
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
.nf
.RS 2
  equals MEMO byte\-for\-byte (UTF\-8); without it every OP_RETURN is refused (unexpected_output).
.RE
.fi
P2PKH/P2PK, plus P2WPKH on btg; every input needs its proving prev_tx), never the BTC sighash.
The transaction (PSBT from tx\-build, a pos\-ntime or zec JSON line from tx\-build, or an unsigned EVM tx) comes from \-\-tx FILE (it is public).
Keys come ONLY on stdin: one per line, WIF or 64\-hex, or JSON lines with wif/private_key/key/secret
(JSON lines without any of those fields, e.g. a reader's "done" line, are skipped).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
1
last status refused
.TP
2
last status bad_input
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ echo x > t; tx\-sign \-\-tx t \-\-expect\-to bc1qrp33g0q5c5txsp9arysrx4k6zdkfs4nce4xj0gdcccefvpysxf3qccfmv3 < /dev/null
# exit 2, last status: bad_input
$ python3 "$R/scripts/e2e\-only/evm\-fixture.py" legacy\-no\-chain\-id > t; printf '%064x\en' 2 | tx\-sign \-\-tx t \-\-chain\-id 1 \-\-expect\-to 0x2B5AD5c4795c026514f8317c7a215E218DcCD6cF
# exit 1, last status: refused
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It may open hostile wallet files and handle secrets: run it sealed and offline (./blocktools run; sealed\-run allows it).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
